WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.920
Hello everyone, welcome back to the Stages of the Path.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.080
Today we're going to review the entire course.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.000
This is good for me, and I wanted to review it myself.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.720
This method of teaching by dividing the video into episodes at different times

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.040
easily loses the continuity of the entire course.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.040
I think we can start from the beginning today and

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.560
review the teachings we covered in this stage of the Stages of the Path.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.080
I plan to review using the "reading images" approach

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:49.040
, the same way we teach ACI teachers.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.040
We require ACI teachers to be able to

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.800
look at a picture and then say what they taught.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.560
Tim, how many pictures have we covered? Probably over a thousand, right?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.120
How many?  There are

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.840
about 500 pictures.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:13.760
Using pictures for exams makes it easy to assess someone.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.920
We just need to show these pictures.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.520
So, I'll challenge everyone.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.680
When I show you a picture,

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.800
I'll give you a little time

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.480
to see if you remember what it's about. This is a

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.160
good way to review the entire course we've taught.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.000
Okay, let's begin.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.040
Please show the first picture, Mr. Sergi.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.080
This picture is a reminder that

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:51.480
we're talking about the stages of practice for intermediate-level practitioners (the middle path).

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.200
They are trying to attain Nirvana.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.880
They are trying to free themselves from the cycle of life and all personal suffering. The

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.840
Buddha taught three trainings here (the three trainings),

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.520
three trainings to help you attain personal Nirvana. The

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.880
third training is understanding emptiness, understanding the "story of the pen" (wisdom). The

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.240
second training is meditation (concentration).

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.160
On a deeper level,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.600
these two trainings can only be done in a very quiet place, at a

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:28.680
specific time of day, when you are truly focused sitting on your meditation mat. On a

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.000
deeper level,

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.840
these two trainings should be done at a special time of day.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.800
And this one is also the foundation of the above two trainings, namely, treating others kindly. It

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.240
can also be called "morality."

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.960
You can call it a moral way of life (morality),

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.120
but ultimately it's about treating others kindly.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.840
This is the foundation.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.720
We can do this training all day long.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.960
It's one of the three extraordinary trainings (the three trainings) in Buddhism,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.920
meaning it can help us attain Nirvana.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.720
We can practice it all day long.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.240
So in this picture,

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.800
you can see Sergi teaching Geshe Michael how to use a computer.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.600
This is one of the best things young people can do for older people.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.960
Next picture,

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.480
see if you remember what this picture is about.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.000
Can you guess?

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.000
This woman is filling out her tax form. This is

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.680
discussed throughout this session of the Stages of the Path teachings. How will this affect her?

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.120
This will make her... a Dharma Master.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:43.240
When I say Dharma Master or Tantric Master,

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.040
I know you'll picture

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.560
a great lama sitting on a throne, wearing a large yellow hat.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:59.080
Maybe they're shaking a vajra bell or striking a small drum (chanting scriptures).

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.040
You're thinking: Oh, that's a Dharma Master.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.200
That's a true Dharma Master.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.080
Or you might think of Nagarjuna in an old photograph,

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.080
looking very mysterious.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.520
But actually, in the Stages of the Path, we learn that,

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.360
like this lady,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.320
she's married, has several children,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:24.080
and she's a Dharma Master, a true Dharma Master.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.680
Pabongka Rinpoche said:

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.200
Don't think that a Dharma Master necessarily sits on a high throne

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.280
reciting some Tantric rituals.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.320
What is this lady doing?

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.440
She was paying taxes.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:45.000
In my country, paying taxes honestly is really difficult. It can

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.240
take weeks. Paying

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.560


00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.760
taxes carefully and completely honestly,

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.560
paying every penny you owe—

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.840
these things made her…

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.520
She underwent the first extraordinary training (precept) of a good person: treating others

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.240
kindly.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.840
This made her a true master of Buddhism.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:12.120
Forget about those pictures of lamas wearing big hats and shaking bells and vajras.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.880
That's easy; everyone can do that.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.600
But treating others kindly is difficult.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:23.200
Adhering to morality and codes of conduct is also difficult.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.000
Next picture.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.200
I'll give you some time. Do you remember what this picture is about?

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.640
The quote from the Stages of the Path is:

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.680
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.320
A person who truly upholds the precepts, who

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:49.080
truly follows the Buddhist guidelines, especially the ten guidelines,

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.920
will shine brightly, truly radiantly.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:06:00.680
A person who healthily, humbly, and modestly strives to keep their promises,

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.560
upholds the ten virtuous deeds, and treats

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.400
others kindly, will have

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.440
a certain peaceful expression on their face.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.560
They are radiating light.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.680
When they enter the room,

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.120
everyone begins to feel better,

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.080
like Tim and Serge.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.480
That is the light of the world. The

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.680
Buddha said: Those people are the light of the world.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.040
There is a saying in Christianity:

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.720
Don't put your candle under the basket.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.280
Let the world see your smiling face.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:42.160
This is the true guiding light of the whole world.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:46.120
Next, picture 4.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.800
This is the cliff.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:58.040
My partner Veronica and I went there to celebrate her birthday.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.000
During this Stages of the Path teaching,

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:08.800
they were discussing sunset. The Tibetan word is NUB PA, which

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:10.480
also means "west"

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.240
because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.800
NUB PA means sunset.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.440
This verb is sad.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:22.840
In Buddhism, this is also a very sad concept.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.400
Its most famous source is at the end of the Abhidharmakośa,

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.080
also known as the Treasury of Higher Wisdom,

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.960
Vasubandhu's *Treasury of Higher Knowledge*, where he says:

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.440
"The sun of the Dharma, the light of the Dharma, will set in this world."

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.080
Our world will lose the light of the Dharma.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.080
This world will go into darkness.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.320
After a certain period, the

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:51.040
Buddha's teachings will disappear from this world.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.320
They will first disappear from human consciousness,

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.280
but will still exist in libraries.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.000
These books will still be in libraries,

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.640
perhaps in libraries that John Brady hasn't discovered yet. After

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.000
that, they will also disappear from libraries

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.320
and cease to exist.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.080
I put this image here

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.200
because Pabongka Rinpoche raised a special point.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.000
He said: If you cannot keep your promises,

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.440
if you cannot treat others with kindness,

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.520
then we can say that the Dharma has left this world. The

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.520
light of the Dharma has left your inner world.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:32.480
In your own heart, the sun has set.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.120
This is really sad

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.240
if we cannot uphold the precepts (that will happen).

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.160
Next image:

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:50.200
Our retreat is called "Love in the Time of Pandemic."

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:57.000
The focus is: When the world is going through very difficult times,

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.320
if you can keep your promises, if

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:02.200
you treat others with kindness,

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.760
when things are causing panic and fear, when the virus is spreading...

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:08.080
We don't know which direction things will take, or how they will develop.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.160
We don't know how many people will die.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:18.200
If you do something kind to others during such a difficult time, the

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.560
seeds will be even stronger.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:24.720
He mentioned that if you remember the five-star Buddha Paradise, it's like

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:27.600
an exceptionally perfect place. It's

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.680
easy to be a good person there.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.120
Everyone there is a good person.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.040
It's not a great achievement, not a big deal.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.920
And the seeds planted by being kind among a group of good people are
n't that strong.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:45.160
When people attack you, when people are worried, be kind.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.040
When everyone is not treating each other kindly,

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:55.440
be the one who stands up and shares things in difficult times. That kind of

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.800
person is extremely pure.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.960
That's immense karma, incredible karma, even more powerful.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.840
I think this pandemic is a very good opportunity.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.000
For all of us, it's a great opportunity to show whether

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.000
we are true Buddhist disciples. Are

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.640
we truly practicing the Bodhisattva path?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.040
Even when things are going badly, will we still help others?  The

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.080
next

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:33.120
image is hard to remember; I can hardly recall it myself.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:39.080
I'll give you some time to try and remember it.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.440
Pabongka Rinpoche quoted some books, and in the

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:50.680
endings of various books,

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:53.080
he quoted a famous prayer:

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:56.200
BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.040
BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG. This

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.520
means, "

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:09.320
May the teachings of His Holiness Lobsang Tsongkhapa spread throughout the world
(especially His Holiness the Venerable One, may the essence of the Holy Teachings shine eternally)."

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.120
You might think:

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:18.120
We should go online and translate the Stages of the Path into multiple languages.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:23.720
We should strive to spread these good words to as many people as possible.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:26.400
This is the last sentence of the prayer, which

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:32.880
also means that after we leave the classroom where the Stages of the Path are taught or after watching the video, we should

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.200
share the Dharma with others.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.840
We should spread the Dharma throughout the world.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:45.680
In this section on the Stages of the Path, Pabongka Rinpoche said: "The

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:52.160
place where you spread the Dharma should be here, in your own heart.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.080
Don't think that spreading the Dharma is just about

00:11:55.080 --> 00:12:00.120
trying to translate videos into more languages.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.720
That's a very important way to spread the Dharma."

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:07.160
But he said: If you spread it in your own heart,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.800
then the Dharma will definitely spread outwards

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.560
because the world comes from your heart,

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.560
in fact, from your heart chakra.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.200
Next, picture 7.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.040
Try to recall what this picture is.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:26.840
I will give you some time.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.240
I really like this theme:

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:43.560
having an intimate relationship with another person, like these two people. In

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.320
my opinion, in Vajrayana,

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.480
this is one of the happiest things that happen to you.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:53.840
This is one of the best things that happen to you.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.160
Anyone can tell you that the

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:01.520
whole world is looking for a partner because it makes people happy.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:05.520
When things are going well, it is one of the greatest happinesses.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.800
This is one of the greatest happinesses you can have.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:14.800
But you and I both know that when things aren't going well,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.040
this is the greatest misfortune in life.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:22.760
Why is this relevant to this lesson?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:31.040
If you uphold morality (observance),

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.280
this is the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.240
But if you break the precepts, the same thing will cause you great pain.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:42.400
Just like having a wonderful woman or man as your partner—

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.120
someone who brings you immense joy

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.040
can also cause you unbearable suffering.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.080
So in this case, the

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:57.680
precepts—the personal practice of kindness and good deeds—are likened to a partner.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.720
He/she can create the best

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.240
or the worst thing in your life—the same person.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.920
Next, picture 8.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.440
This picture is difficult to understand; see if you remember it.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.480
I'll take a small sip of green juice first.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.040
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:35.160
Actually, this represents breaking a promise.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.040
Pulling out this weed represents breaking a promise.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:46.680
Why is destroying this plant breaking a promise?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.560
If you are a gardener,

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:56.400
you know you should pull weeds before the seeds sprout.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.080
If you wait until the seeds are almost falling off

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.600
before pulling up a plant,

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.920
you will have sown thousands more seeds.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.680
The following month, the following year, thousands upon thousands of weeds will grow.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.800
So you must remove these weeds early.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:23.480
This refers to a very extreme statement made by the Buddha:

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:27.600
DGE SLONG DAG SROG
DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I It is

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:33.440
better to die than to break a vow.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:34.960
Why?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
When you break a vow,

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.360
you are activating seeds that

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.480
will continue to sow seeds for many lifetimes.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:51.080
If you die, you destroy a complex of body and consciousness.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.840
If you die, you destroy a very useful temple—

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:59.800
a tangible temple and consciousness; you lose a complex.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.480
But if you break a promise (break a vow), you

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:06.400
lose many complexes of body and consciousness.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.320
You destroy bodies and consciousness for many lifetimes.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.920
You are like setting seeds in motion;

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.720
they will destroy lives for many lifetimes.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:21.400
The Buddha said: "I would rather die than break a vow."

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:33.040
When he said he would rather die than break a vow,
he wasn't using a metaphor; he was speaking the truth.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:38.040
There's a joke in the Stages of the Path:

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:43.000
We vow never to give up Bodhicitta,

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:46.200
even at the cost of our lives.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:53.960
There's a famous saying: We spend our whole lives waiting to be

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:58.560
imprisoned by some evil person

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:04.680
who holds a knife and says: "Either give up your Bodhisattva vows, or you die today."

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:06.120
Then we say: "

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.960
I choose to die,"

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.520
and then they kill us.

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:15.280
I think all of us have been waiting for this moment since we received our vows.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:19.720
We've been waiting for such a person to threaten us with a knife.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.240
But in reality, we are the ones holding the knife. We

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:25.680
threaten our Bodhisattva vows every day.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:29.960
We have to make this decision every day:

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:34.000
whether to carefully uphold our vows.

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:39.480
It's hard to find someone like that—they lock you up in jail and say, "

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:42.920
If you don't renounce your Bodhisattva vows, I'll kill you."

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.040
Next picture.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:51.520
See if you remember.

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:56.680
I'll give you some time to try and recall.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.200
This represents…

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:10.440
We have a mixed-nut translation team.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.920
We were previously translating an ancient Vinaya text, the

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:18.080
Sangha Vinaya, the Sangha and Nun Vinaya. The

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:21.080
text mentions this precept:

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:26.560
There is a tradition that we should not…

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.120
When you ordain as a monk or nun, you

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:33.680
receive a robe, a small Buddha statue,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.040
and a filter.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:41.280
In ancient India, you were supposed to carry this filter with you.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:44.800
If you drink water from a stream, you

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.080
should filter the water first

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:51.320
to ensure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:57.000
We mentioned a famous tradition in the Vinaya:

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:00.680
if several monks are going to find water and

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.840
go to a stream to fetch water,

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:09.240
they should choose the best monk to check the water.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.120
Don't choose the one who doesn't care about small insects.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.080
Try to find the one who loves small insects and

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.720
have them check the water, because they will be more careful.

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:23.400
What's the key point?

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.920
We seem to have discussed some ecological precepts.

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:34.040
Monks and nuns shouldn't even break the green leaves of plants

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:39.040
because that's the home of small creatures. This means

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:44.400
observing even the smallest precepts

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:46.160
very strictly,

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:51.000
because the results multiply exponentially.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:58.080
Therefore, it's important to observe morality at a very subtle, very nuanced level.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:01.400
But don't be nitpicky.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.160
If I were to write about the Bodhisattva precepts,

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:06.040
I would add an extra one:

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.880
Don't constantly talk about your Bodhisattva precepts.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.800
Nothing is more annoying

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:20.080
than someone telling you they're observing them, so it has to be so bothersome.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:25.560
So, observe the precepts happily, joyfully, but not excessively.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:27.920
Don't bother others with your precepts

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.840
because precepts aren't meant to bother others. Observe the

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.080
small precepts quietly. Observe them

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.520
yourself, don't announce them widely.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.600
There's an Islamic saying: "

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:44.000
The left hand should not let the right hand know what it's doing." This

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:48.560
means: Don't publicize your precepts everywhere, just observe them quietly.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.720
Observe the precepts at a subtle level.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.040
Next picture.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:10.480
This concept is: Treat others kindly like planting a tree.

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:16.160
Today I went to the Peach Tree Cafe to check some things.

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:22.560
When Chen Tang, Xiaoping, and I first started the "Peach Tree Morning Show,"

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:26.080
we planted a peach tree there.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:30.400
I want to tell everyone that three peaches have grown on the tree this week.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:34.080
We have peaches now. This

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:40.160
means that if you take good care of your basic practice, take good care of the foundation, and

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.880
cultivate good karma

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:47.920
through keeping precepts and treating others kindly, it

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.200
will grow into a tree.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:54.680
That peach tree was planted about five months ago and

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.040
has already begun to provide a lot of fruit.

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:03.040
If you don't take good care of it when it's small, you

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.600
won't get anything.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:09.040
If you take good care of your Buddhist practice foundation, which

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.000
is to treat others kindly,

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.120
then there will be thousands upon thousands of fruits.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:17.280
They will grow into very large trees...

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:21.040
They will grow into trees and produce peaches every year.

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:24.600
Then you will harvest peaches for many years.

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:29.560
This child carefully protects the buds.

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.200
Guard your morality.

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:34.920
Next picture.

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:38.400
If I remember correctly, there

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:45.080
are four conditions that can lead you to break your vows.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.560
If you have taken the Bodhisattva vows, or the

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.920
Pratimoksha vows,

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:54.560
or even the Vajrayana secret vows,

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:57.480
I think there are four of them.

00:22:57.480 --> 00:22:58.840
Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed...

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:00.280
No, maybe more than that.

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:04.880
But anyway, there are indeed some conditions that can help you break your vows.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:09.240
If you want to break your vows, here are a few special ways. The

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:11.080
first one is...

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:16.440
If you don't know what the precepts are,

00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:18.120
this is a good way to break them.

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:22.440
If you want to break them, don't learn them.

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:27.360
One of the things I hate most, and many things about Buddhism that I dislike, is when

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:33.800
teachers give initiations, lots of initiations,

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:41.040
but don't explain to the recipients that they've just given precepts.

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:45.520
When you receive an initiation, you also receive hundreds of precepts,

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.320
and if you don't know these precepts, you'll break them.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:55.760
Before an initiation, the teacher has a responsibility to train you on the relevant precepts.

00:23:56.320 --> 00:23:58.720
If they don't say they'll explain,

00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:01.840
I won't receive an initiation from them. The

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.560
best way to break a precept is,

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:07.400
first, not understanding the precepts.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:10.240
Look at the recipe before cooking.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:13.200
Veronica always says this when I cook.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.160
Next picture:

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:23.360
A lady is saying, "It's no big deal."

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:27.720
That precept is about

00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:34.160
not breaking green plants without praying. Come on, that's a bit much. That's a bit

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:37.240


00:24:37.240 --> 00:24:41.640
excessive, not that important.

00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:43.000
It's just a few small insects.

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.560
They might occasionally use that leaf as a roof. It's not a big

00:24:48.560 --> 00:24:50.040
deal. The

00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:55.760
second important way to break a precept is to have this attitude:

00:24:55.760 --> 00:24:59.920
"Oh, that one isn't very important; I'm upholding important precepts."

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:02.120
Next picture:

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:08.040
If we had Klesha...  It

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:15.120
means: If you let certain negative emotions run rampant in your mind,

00:25:15.120 --> 00:25:17.080
this is a good way to break your vows. Getting

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:21.080
annoyed by others,

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:26.280
or being obsessed with getting something or money, or being

00:25:26.920 --> 00:25:29.760
attracted to Netflix (a movie website) at night.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:34.480
By the way, there's nothing wrong with watching Netflix videos. What

00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:41.800
I'm saying is, hurting others because you want to go home and watch Netflix is

00:25:41.800 --> 00:25:43.000
a problem.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.920
This is called "gang fight".

00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:49.160
What's the story?

00:25:52.480 --> 00:25:56.400
Head straight for the biggest leader of the other group.

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.320
Find out who the leader is.

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:04.080
Don't speak, don't negotiate, don't shout at each other.

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:07.360
Just walk up to him and strike him on the head.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:10.800
Then the entire gang will collapse.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:15.080
Identify your worst bad habit and

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:20.960
pursue it first; this is the method of discipline. Next

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:23.000
picture. By the

00:26:26.840 --> 00:26:31.000
way, at my age—

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.760
I'm not trying to tell you how old I am—

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:37.080
all the things that young people love

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:41.760
seem ridiculous to someone my age.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:46.000
I have some experience with

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.240
things like:

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:51.240
Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world.

00:26:51.400 --> 00:26:54.200
He's the most handsome man in the world.

00:26:54.440 --> 00:27:01.280
First of all, my brother once said something very funny:

00:27:01.440 --> 00:27:02.200
He said, "Do you like that girl?"

00:27:02.280 --> 00:27:03.320
I said: Yes.

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.320
He said: Do you want to spend your life with her?

00:27:05.320 --> 00:27:05.960
I said: Yes.

00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:09.000
He said: Let's find out about her mother first,

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:11.240
see what her mother looks like.

00:27:11.240 --> 00:27:14.080
I said: Her mother is very ugly, overweight.

00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:16.920
She looks very tired and scary.

00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:21.840
Then he said: What do you think her mother looked like when she was young?

00:27:21.840 --> 00:27:23.560
So think about it.

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:30.000
If you're fixated on someone's appearance,

00:27:30.400 --> 00:27:32.720
or external conditions,

00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:35.400
or things that aren't important to them,

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:38.680
those things change. You'll see them get sick,

00:27:38.720 --> 00:27:44.000
see them age, see them have diarrhea and vomit.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:45.840
If you're not so lucky,

00:27:45.840 --> 00:27:48.920
you might even sometimes see their internal organs during surgery.

00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:52.120
Don't deceive yourself:

00:27:52.680 --> 00:27:59.000
thinking it's worth hurting someone to get the most beautiful woman or man.

00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:01.200
It's not worth it. It

00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:04.120
won't last.

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:09.160
Having a relationship is good, but get it for a good reason. Next.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:11.200


00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.880
If you have a problem with getting angry

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.160
or are easily angered,

00:28:18.320 --> 00:28:23.960
then imagine giving this person something they want.

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:25.960
This is called maitre-

00:28:26.120 --> 00:28:27.480
jampa-

00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:28.120
love.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:31.040
Visualize, try to imagine

00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:36.000
how wonderful it would be to give them what they love and want. Try to

00:28:36.160 --> 00:28:37.960
cultivate this attitude.

00:28:37.960 --> 00:28:42.760
If you're unfriendly to another person,

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.680
then fantasize, that is, meditate,

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:51.000
imagine giving them something they really like.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
Next.

00:28:54.040 --> 00:28:57.720
I'll give you some time.

00:28:57.720 --> 00:29:01.080
I bet you can't remember what this picture is.

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:05.120
Tim is cheating (rewind).

00:29:07.480 --> 00:29:10.320
What is this picture?

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:14.240
This image is about arrogance.

00:29:15.040 --> 00:29:18.840
Arrogance can also be an obstacle to upholding precepts.

00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:24.400
This book talks about the

00:29:24.600 --> 00:29:29.080
most common kind of arrogance in monasteries, which

00:29:29.080 --> 00:29:37.120
is how much you know about the scriptures and how many facts you've collected in your life.

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.600
I really enjoy this: collecting obscure Buddhist facts. The

00:29:41.800 --> 00:29:47.160
more you collect, the more special you feel.

00:29:48.160 --> 00:29:51.720
Pabongka Rinpoche said: All the Buddhist teachings you've studied in your life,

00:29:51.720 --> 00:29:52.960
all the things you've memorized,

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:54.720
all the things you've debated, all the

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:57.480
Geshe degrees you've obtained—

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:02.000
compared to the things you still don't know,

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:03.400
you know very little.

00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:08.000
You're like a tiny worm in the ocean.

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:12.600
Sometimes you go out and look up at the stars.

00:30:13.400 --> 00:30:16.080
Many stars have planets orbiting them. There are

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:21.240
people on those planets, and we need to know a lot about them. What

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.480
we know, what

00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:27.240
we're proud of,

00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:33.880
is only a very, very small part of what we can understand.

00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:37.200
So don't be arrogant. The

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.200


00:30:42.120 --> 00:30:50.040


00:30:50.120 --> 00:30:52.000


00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:58.400
next image is one of the temptations that cause you to break precepts, break promises, or violate morality. One of the temptations that prevents you from reaching Nirvana, the second level of the path—personal Nirvana,

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:01.480
is (not) understanding emptiness, (not) studying emptiness.

00:31:01.680 --> 00:31:03.680
If you recognize the

00:31:03.840 --> 00:31:09.080
harsh things others have done to you...  If it

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:13.240
comes directly from what you did last week,

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:16.600
then you won't make a big mistake.

00:31:17.040 --> 00:31:22.960
The more you learn about emptiness, the more you learn about cause and effect, dependent origination—meaning

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:26.160
this person comes from my seeds—

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:32.600
then it will be easier for you to keep the precepts.

00:31:32.600 --> 00:31:34.520
So learn, learn, and learn some more.

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:41.800
I had a teacher, an elderly teacher from Inner Mongolia,

00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:46.480
very old, suffering from tuberculosis.

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.680
He once said:

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:54.680
He's good, you're proud, you have a lot to be proud of.

00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:56.680
Graduated from Princeton University,

00:31:57.080 --> 00:31:58.720
then got a Geshe degree.

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:00.800
These are all very useful, very useful.

00:32:01.760 --> 00:32:04.360
You'll work harder to push yourself,

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:06.440
to make yourself look smart.

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:11.600
That's lucky, but later try to give up these things and

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:14.160
just learn to be a good person. It's

00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:16.080
funny.

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:19.680
He gave me the Adam (translated) scripture on his deathbed.

00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:21.760
I still remember it. Next

00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:26.160
picture.

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:30.320
Technically, this is the fourth cause.

00:32:31.760 --> 00:32:36.720
One of the causes that makes you break your vows or break your promises is:

00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:40.120
In modern society, when you're busy, it's

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:44.720
hard to keep your consciousness on the precepts.

00:32:44.720 --> 00:32:47.000
Things are moving so fast.

00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:49.520
There are thousands of things to see on the internet.

00:32:50.280 --> 00:32:53.000
Life changes so quickly that it's

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:58.640
hard to maintain this self-awareness: Have

00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:03.840
I broken my vows?  Did I do anything to hurt others?

00:33:04.240 --> 00:33:08.680
You need to slow down a bit and return to the precepts. Maintain a certain sensitivity to the

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:19.200
fact that you've promised yourself not to hurt others. The


00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:24.160
busier you are, the more careful you need to be.

00:33:24.560 --> 00:33:31.000
When you're busy, it's even easy to get angry with your partner.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.800
They try to tell you something.

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:38.160
You're busy handling 10 things at work.

00:33:38.160 --> 00:33:41.720
You might say, "I don't have time to listen to you right now." "My

00:33:42.080 --> 00:33:45.960
boss assigned me 10 things."

00:33:46.760 --> 00:33:49.440
These are precisely the times you should slow down,

00:33:49.440 --> 00:33:51.200
return to the precepts, and

00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:55.000
not forget your promise to be kind to others. Even if you're

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:58.320
stressed, busy,

00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:03.200
or breaking some business promises, it's

00:34:03.320 --> 00:34:10.040
better than being tense, anxious, and unfriendly to others,

00:34:10.440 --> 00:34:14.720
even if it means not paying bills, missing business meetings,

00:34:15.320 --> 00:34:17.920
or not putting in your best effort at work.

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:23.080
If it helps you stay clear-headed, then it's better to do so.

00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:27.080
Next picture:

00:34:27.280 --> 00:34:32.160
This woman is buying something useless in a store.

00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:35.600
See if you can remember this story.

00:34:36.800 --> 00:34:39.240
She said, "Oh, this box is so pretty!"

00:34:39.240 --> 00:34:42.400
She went to a department store and bought this box.

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:45.080
What was that home goods store called?  Is this a

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.960
place to buy things?  Like Crate and Barrel,

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:50.920
she went to a Crate and Barrel store in the US and

00:34:50.920 --> 00:34:54.160
said, "Oh, my husband will love this box."

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:57.960
She had no idea what the box was for,

00:34:58.160 --> 00:35:00.800
but she just wanted to take it home.

00:35:04.720 --> 00:35:07.080
When she got home, her husband said, "Are

00:35:07.080 --> 00:35:09.920
you crazy?"  This little box is completely useless.

00:35:09.920 --> 00:35:12.040
We already have enough junk at home. Should she

00:35:12.160 --> 00:35:15.520
return it and get a refund?

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:22.200
Should she go back to the gas station and try to return it?

00:35:24.040 --> 00:35:26.920
No, this box wasn't bought from there.

00:35:26.920 --> 00:35:30.960
That's obvious, but we still have to say this: what

00:35:31.200 --> 00:35:33.920
if you bought a useless box

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:36.440
because you liked it, and you thought your husband would like it too,

00:35:36.440 --> 00:35:39.000
but he doesn't? What does it mean if

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.560
he tells you to return it,

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:44.840
but not somewhere else, but

00:35:44.840 --> 00:35:46.720
back to where you bought it

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:48.720
?

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:58.080
You have to pay me.

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:03.280
When you break the precepts and should repent,

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:06.720
try to find the person who gave you the precepts and

00:36:07.080 --> 00:36:12.120
try to repent in front of that person. Is it okay to repent

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:15.960
at home by yourself?

00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:22.680
Generally speaking, it's not allowed if you received the precepts from someone else.

00:36:23.080 --> 00:36:27.280
If you didn't receive the precepts from someone else, you might be able to repent

00:36:27.400 --> 00:36:32.040
at home in front of a Buddha statue or something similar.

00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:34.240
In extreme cases, that's fine.

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:36.240
But generally speaking,

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:39.840
if you can find the person who gave you the precepts,

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:43.800
open your heart and repent to them, even if it's a bit shameless, okay?

00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:45.800
Anyway, we're all shameless these days,

00:36:45.840 --> 00:36:48.080
so when you're honest about your vows, be a little brazen and

00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:49.960
say: "Whatever." Go

00:36:49.960 --> 00:36:53.080
straight to your teacher and say, "I stupidly broke this vow."

00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:55.960
Then your teacher will say, "Wow, that's terrible."

00:36:55.960 --> 00:36:57.400
You'll say, "Yeah, yeah," and that's it. You'll

00:36:57.400 --> 00:37:02.480
feel so clean, so wonderful.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:06.160
You can be a little shy about many things in life,

00:37:06.160 --> 00:37:08.000
but never be ashamed of breaking your vows (confess).

00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:11.000
If you've broken a vow, tell someone.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:12.680
And when you do that, you've cleared the negative seed, and the

00:37:12.680 --> 00:37:14.120
problem is solved.

00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:18.400
If you cling to it or keep it a secret,

00:37:18.400 --> 00:37:21.720
and if you spend more energy hiding it instead of admitting your mistake,

00:37:21.720 --> 00:37:23.640
that's incredibly foolish,

00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:26.600
and you won't feel good. You won't feel clean.

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:31.760
Be honest with your teacher: "I have this problem, I have this bad habit." The

00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:37.720
karma will be crushed, the seed will be crushed.

00:37:38.640 --> 00:37:42.280
Your teacher will say, "I've heard that before, you told me before,

00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:45.000
but you have to keep going, keep telling them."

00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:50.320
Next picture.

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:54.320
This is about… wait, do you remember?

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:07.720
Here, once again, it's about respecting the precepts in small details.

00:38:07.720 --> 00:38:13.680
This is actually about a precept for monks: they should brush their teeth

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:16.320
with a stick called a SO SHING.

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:19.080
This is a stick you use to clean your teeth.

00:38:19.080 --> 00:38:21.280
You just need to cut it down from a tree, and then you can use it. It

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.160
's a toothbrush. What's being

00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:29.360
said here is: monks should have their own toothbrushes, and you should brush your teeth.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.040
This seems like a small thing. Wait

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:37.000
, I'm trying hard to uphold my Tantric vows, practicing the

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:38.920
Dharma to go to Amitabha's Pure Land,

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:41.480
and protecting all sentient beings.

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:44.240
Then the Buddha says: Okay, but before you go there,

00:38:44.240 --> 00:38:46.080
please brush your teeth every day, okay?

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:49.080
You might think: those aren't really important precepts.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:53.800
But it's precisely these small things that create the Buddha's Pure Land.

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:59.800
These are things Bodhisattvas often do—small things of kindness towards others.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:05.200
Of course, if everyone in the world could do that, they would

00:39:05.200 --> 00:39:07.560
stop a nuclear war or something similar;

00:39:07.600 --> 00:39:09.000
that's obvious.

00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:12.120
But are you a good enough person to

00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:18.800
even think about not letting others smell your breath, afraid of making them uncomfortable?

00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:23.960
If you are very sensitive to any small things that might hurt others, then

00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:27.200
we can say—you uphold your morality (precepts).

00:39:28.160 --> 00:39:36.160
So, it is these small details that ultimately adorn your Pure Land. You

00:39:36.280 --> 00:39:37.560
can see this in the next picture.

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:46.160
This person is decorating a Christmas tree.

00:39:48.200 --> 00:39:50.080
I don't know if you've ever decorated a Christmas tree,

00:39:50.080 --> 00:39:52.240
but for those of us who grew up in Christian tradition, our

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
parents would have us decorate Christmas trees.

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:58.120
When putting on the last decoration,

00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:02.080
something cool happens.

00:40:02.680 --> 00:40:05.480
Everyone looks at the tree and says: "Done!"

00:40:05.480 --> 00:40:07.240
They say: "Yes, finished!"

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:11.480
He says: "Wait a minute, we need to put one more over there."

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:17.960
This Christmas tree (the last decoration) is a toothbrush.

00:40:17.960 --> 00:40:22.000
This is the final detail that leads to your Buddhahood.

00:40:22.240 --> 00:40:28.720
It is these small things that create Buddhahood,

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:31.000
not those major events, not those big things.

00:40:31.120 --> 00:40:39.040
It is the attention to small details that make others happy that makes Buddha. Next,

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:43.560


00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:49.040
see if you remember this, here's a hint
—Yamantika.

00:40:57.000 --> 00:41:01.120
This is a famous story from the Stages of the Path to Enlightenment.

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:06.040
Monks and nuns are supposed to confess twice a month,

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:11.080
openly admitting the mistakes they have made.

00:41:13.080 --> 00:41:15.080
The teacher said, "

00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:18.320
They strike the gunty, they strike that gunty. It

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:22.600
's a special piece of wood, it looks insignificant.

00:41:23.200 --> 00:41:27.600
Then you hit it with another small stick, making a thud, thud, thud sound.

00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:33.400
Before metal became widespread, this was an ancient bell.

00:41:33.400 --> 00:41:37.120
They would strike a wooden board.

00:41:37.480 --> 00:41:40.080
When you hear that sound, you have to make a confession.

00:41:40.080 --> 00:41:41.360
They still do that now."

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:44.040
I made a gunty for my teacher, he wanted one.

00:41:45.200 --> 00:41:47.560
We made one according to the correct size.

00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:49.600
There are many rules for making it.

00:41:49.880 --> 00:41:51.880
When you hear the sound of the gunty,

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:54.240
you should... put it here.

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:57.360
You hold it like this, and then strike it like this.

00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:01.520
Then all the monks and nuns have to make confessions. The

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:05.760
teacher said: "Hey, they've struck that gunty, let's go." The

00:42:06.520 --> 00:42:09.200
student said: "No, I'm not going to make a confession today."

00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:12.160
The teacher said: "What?"

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:17.200
Making a confession is one of the main commitments of a monk.

00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:19.120
The teacher asked: What are you saying?

00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:20.600
He said, "I don't need to go today."

00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:24.080
The teacher asked, "What do you mean by saying you don't need to go today?"  The

00:42:24.120 --> 00:42:27.920
student said: "Have you forgotten that you gave me the Vajrabhairava empowerment yesterday?"

00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:30.960
I am Vajrabhairava, I have attained Buddhahood,

00:42:30.960 --> 00:42:33.080
I no longer need to go to confession ceremonies.

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:36.160
The teacher then grabbed his ear and

00:42:36.160 --> 00:42:38.160
said: What are you?  !  Are you Vajrabhairava?

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:43.240
Vajrabhairava also needs to go to confession with me, right away!

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:48.160
This means:
Don't tell me you're a great practitioner of Tantra, that

00:42:49.080 --> 00:42:54.040
you've transcended morality, and that you now have a higher perspective.

00:42:54.800 --> 00:42:57.960
That idea is completely wrong!

00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:02.040
If you receive a secret empowerment,

00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:05.600
then you should make confessions every morning, and so on.

00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:08.400
You should do this more often than others

00:43:08.400 --> 00:43:12.360
because it will empower your Tantric practice. That is,

00:43:12.600 --> 00:43:17.080
being kind to others and being honest when you make mistakes. Next image:

00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:19.480


00:43:22.520 --> 00:43:24.920
This is a sad picture.

00:43:24.920 --> 00:43:30.080
We always think that morality is the foundation of our practice, the basis of our

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:32.680
practice.

00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:35.960
However, Pabongka Rinpoche turned it around in a way.

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:38.800
This picture is perfect.

00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:42.240
He said: Imagine an apple tree.

00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:46.160
Someone cut it in half. Actually, he used a palm tree as an example.

00:43:47.400 --> 00:43:52.360
Someone is cutting down the tree. They cut off the crown.

00:43:52.720 --> 00:43:55.080
Now you can't get leaves. Not a

00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:58.040
single leaf can grow.

00:43:58.320 --> 00:44:00.440
Therefore, you can't get flowers either.

00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:05.080
Therefore, you can't harvest the fruit that comes from the flowers.

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:07.880
You will get nothing.

00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:13.560
If a person is not kind to others day after day, moment by moment,

00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:18.840
they cut off all the opportunities to harvest the

00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:23.560
beautiful fruit that comes from practice.

00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:25.200
Next image:

00:44:31.800 --> 00:44:35.200
This idea comes from something my teacher once asked me. I'm

00:44:37.160 --> 00:44:39.480
sorry, I asked my teacher.

00:44:39.480 --> 00:44:43.080
I don't know if you remember, but I asked him: The

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:49.200
first of the five paths—the path of accumulation.

00:44:51.520 --> 00:44:55.440
When you personally encounter a calamity, you reach the first path.

00:44:55.840 --> 00:44:59.080
But if you are in the Bodhisattva path, you only

00:44:59.400 --> 00:45:01.560
reach the first path when you attain Bodhicitta.

00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:05.680
So I ask: I don't understand what calamities are associated with Bodhicitta?

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:12.720
He said: No, no, that theme (the path of accumulation in the Bodhisattva path) is still calamity. It's

00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:17.040
just that it's a calamity for all sentient beings.

00:45:17.040 --> 00:45:22.080
All sentient beings in the universe have the same calamity.

00:45:23.440 --> 00:45:30.000
That common calamity is the beginning of the five paths.

00:45:30.160 --> 00:45:35.480
For a Bodhisattva, contemplating that calamity is the beginning of the five paths.

00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:37.120
So really, it's all the same.

00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:41.760
This little dog is in pain, but now all the little dogs in the basket are in pain.

00:45:44.040 --> 00:45:46.040
We are all in the same boat.

00:45:46.040 --> 00:45:48.800
That is the beginning of Bodhicitta.

00:45:52.280 --> 00:45:53.560
Next picture: There's someone

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.200
shaking hands with someone in an office.

00:45:58.920 --> 00:46:02.280
I imagine: the lady is introducing them.

00:46:02.280 --> 00:46:05.200
This is Joe, he works in the advertising department.

00:46:05.200 --> 00:46:08.800
This is Sam, he works in the computer department.

00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:11.400
They shake hands with each other. Do

00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:14.040
you remember what this theme is?

00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:22.680
This is a really fun exercise.

00:46:22.680 --> 00:46:24.520
We should close our eyes and

00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:28.160
think about the person we annoy the most, and

00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:31.320
see if we make ourselves feel annoyed. The

00:46:31.600 --> 00:46:33.960
problem with this kind of exercise is:

00:46:33.960 --> 00:46:36.240
after ten minutes, you forget it's just an exercise and

00:46:37.080 --> 00:46:39.080
you actually start to feel annoyed!

00:46:40.160 --> 00:46:42.160
Let me see if I can make myself upset.

00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:44.160
What do you do?

00:46:44.160 --> 00:46:46.160
I need to think about the person who caused me trouble this week.

00:46:46.160 --> 00:46:47.680
"Okay, let's begin."

00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:50.680
Then, slowly, this person starts to tremble.

00:46:50.680 --> 00:46:52.320
You ask, "What's wrong?"

00:46:52.480 --> 00:46:54.240
"I'm getting upset."

00:46:54.240 --> 00:46:56.040
The experiment is a success.

00:46:57.600 --> 00:47:00.640
If it were your teacher, they would say,

00:47:01.080 --> 00:47:05.000
"Check how you felt when you first started thinking about this person." What did that

00:47:06.040 --> 00:47:08.600
feel like?  What are you feeling in your heart?

00:47:09.480 --> 00:47:13.040
I don't know how you will feel, but my heart feels a little uncomfortable.

00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:17.960
When I think about someone or a problem that bothers me,

00:47:18.600 --> 00:47:23.080
I start to feel a little uncomfortable here or there.

00:47:23.680 --> 00:47:29.560
I deliberately create tension in my body.

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:34.040
He said: Let's do an exercise:

00:47:34.040 --> 00:47:36.920
Try to induce some tension in your mind.

00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:40.320
Then look at that tension and understand it,

00:47:40.320 --> 00:47:42.040
as if you are shaking hands with someone.

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:46.600
Start to understand what that feels like.

00:47:47.000 --> 00:47:53.000
When the trouble, the negative emotion, first comes to your mind,

00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:54.240
continue this exercise.

00:47:55.200 --> 00:47:58.320
Once you feel better and forget about that person,

00:47:58.400 --> 00:47:59.520
think about them again and see

00:48:00.200 --> 00:48:01.840
if you feel upset again.

00:48:01.880 --> 00:48:03.400
See if you become upset again.

00:48:04.040 --> 00:48:06.440
Try to familiarize yourself with this feeling and shake hands with it.

00:48:06.440 --> 00:48:09.120
"Hi, I'm Geshe Michael." "

00:48:09.120 --> 00:48:10.760
Hi, what's your name?"

00:48:11.080 --> 00:48:14.040
"I'm starting to feel upset about this person."

00:48:14.080 --> 00:48:17.000
"It's nice to meet you, now I know what you look like."

00:48:17.680 --> 00:48:21.200
"Now I can be wary of you, I can avoid you from now on."

00:48:21.840 --> 00:48:23.840
Next.

00:48:28.240 --> 00:48:30.920
This one is called Visiting the Center of the Sun. The

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:37.960
theme of this stage of the path is "Love in the Time of Pandemic." The

00:48:41.080 --> 00:48:44.320
virus is a big deal; it has spread all over the world.

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:48.320
I've lived for a long time, and I thought I had seen everything.

00:48:49.080 --> 00:48:54.960
After I turned 60, I thought nothing new would happen anymore.

00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:57.400
I was prepared for anything that was going to happen.

00:48:58.320 --> 00:49:02.320
I'd seen it all, nothing could bother me anymore.

00:49:02.320 --> 00:49:06.040
Then this virus came, threatening everyone in the world.

00:49:06.600 --> 00:49:11.080
I thought: Wow, this is huge, it's all over the planet.

00:49:13.560 --> 00:49:17.000
I don't know if you've ever experienced this, but it happened to me.

00:49:17.280 --> 00:49:22.480
This might be the ninth unwholesome action, referring to morbid expectations. Taking pleasure in

00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:25.680
other people's misfortunes.

00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:31.160
When I heard that famous, particularly annoying person was sick,

00:49:32.120 --> 00:49:37.080
I certainly didn't wish them dead or anything, but...

00:49:37.960 --> 00:49:42.280
I would think: See, I said it—it's terrible to be a bad person.

00:49:43.000 --> 00:49:46.040
Then I caught myself thinking this.

00:49:47.080 --> 00:49:49.120
This feels huge. It

00:49:49.480 --> 00:49:56.120
seems like this problem has spread all over the planet.

00:49:57.080 --> 00:50:02.040
This feels overwhelming.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:08.040
But after 10 years of studying the stages of the path, we've just entered...

00:50:08.040 --> 00:50:12.840
We've just entered the path of the superior being (the path of higher beings).

00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:20.160
We're about to begin learning the concept of Bodhicitta.

00:50:20.160 --> 00:50:21.200
What is Bodhicitta?  It

00:50:21.280 --> 00:50:23.120
doesn't refer to the consciousness of enlightenment.

00:50:23.120 --> 00:50:27.000
Forget that terrible translation,

00:50:27.960 --> 00:50:34.520
it's utterly awful. It refers to a wish—I want to become a Buddha so that I can help all beings. There is a

00:50:35.760 --> 00:50:37.960
direct experience of it, the same way as

00:50:38.520 --> 00:50:41.600
directly experiencing emptiness.

00:50:41.600 --> 00:50:49.320
Those parallel experiences are what we must go through in this life.

00:50:49.960 --> 00:50:53.080
Again, it must happen in meditation.

00:50:54.040 --> 00:50:57.520
We have described something extraordinary...

00:50:57.520 --> 00:51:00.960
What do you call it?  ...A breakthrough,

00:51:02.400 --> 00:51:06.040
an introductory experience.

00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:11.720
It happens when you enter a deep meditative state

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:15.480
because time and space both originate from seeds.

00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:17.760
If you can manage these seeds,

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:25.600
you can compress time and space in less than half an hour of meditation.

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:31.080
You can truly visit every living being in the universe,

00:51:31.720 --> 00:51:34.440
including animals, insects, birds, and fish.

00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:41.920
In just half an hour, you can communicate one-on-one with each of them.

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:44.920
You can make commitments to each of them.

00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:50.160
You meet them, and you see that they are all suffering,

00:51:50.200 --> 00:51:55.840
each going through a difficult time, constantly worrying about the future.

00:51:56.400 --> 00:51:58.320
You can go to each one individually and say,

00:51:59.080 --> 00:52:01.880
"I will handle this, relax."

00:52:01.960 --> 00:52:04.560
I started working when I was in college.

00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:06.400
I received a scholarship,

00:52:06.400 --> 00:52:08.440
but they said: You must work a certain number of hours each week.

00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:11.000
I later found out it was 30 hours a week.

00:52:13.600 --> 00:52:15.200
I had to drive a truck.

00:52:16.320 --> 00:52:18.840
Actually, they first took me to a coffee shop.

00:52:18.840 --> 00:52:21.200
They said: You have to mop the floor in the coffee shop.

00:52:21.280 --> 00:52:24.920
I gave up after less than 10 hours; I gave up on the first day.

00:52:25.960 --> 00:52:27.760
Then they said: You can drive a truck.

00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:29.760
I said: That sounds fun, I'll drive a truck.

00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:33.520
I drove a truck for 5 years.

00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:37.560
One of us

00:52:37.960 --> 00:52:42.960
was a permanent employee at the university named John Strong.

00:52:43.320 --> 00:52:49.240
His name was John Strong; he was Polish, 7 feet tall, and very strong.

00:52:50.800 --> 00:52:54.040
Everyone was afraid of him when they saw him, very afraid of him,

00:52:54.040 --> 00:52:56.120
but he was a very good person.

00:52:57.000 --> 00:53:02.840
He would bring donuts to work. He was from Trenton, New Jersey.

00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:08.280
He would do the best things for us, and he would always protect us. One

00:53:08.280 --> 00:53:10.440
day we crashed a truck in two.

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:13.840
We crashed the truck into a tree, and then the truck broke in two.

00:53:14.440 --> 00:53:19.560
He covered for us: "Oh, these screws weren't very tight.

00:53:19.560 --> 00:53:23.400
I don't know how, the truck just split open. Don't blame these guys.

00:53:24.160 --> 00:53:26.160
Don't blame these young people.

00:53:26.440 --> 00:53:28.440
They were just driving."

00:53:28.920 --> 00:53:30.080
Then he winked at us and

00:53:30.080 --> 00:53:33.080
said, "I'll protect you. I'll protect all of you."

00:53:34.400 --> 00:53:37.040
When I contemplate Bodhicitta, I always think of him.

00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:42.000
You will directly see every sentient being in the universe.

00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:46.600
Then you will say: "John will protect you. I will protect you. Don't worry. Don't

00:53:47.200 --> 00:53:49.280
worry, I'll protect you."

00:53:50.320 --> 00:53:52.880
This is Bodhicitta. You should have this experience.

00:53:52.880 --> 00:53:55.680
You should strive to have this experience. You must meditate.

00:53:56.240 --> 00:53:58.080
You must learn Bodhicitta.

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:00.320
You must learn the part about Bodhicitta in the Stages of the Path.

00:54:01.360 --> 00:54:03.400
You must do all these steps,

00:54:04.480 --> 00:54:06.480
such as exchanging self and others.

00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:11.120
One day you will have this experience. You will meet every sentient being.

00:54:11.840 --> 00:54:15.280
You would say to them: I'll take care of you, don't worry, I'll protect you.

00:54:15.400 --> 00:54:20.040
Mike will take care of you, or Tim, or Serge. Don't

00:54:20.600 --> 00:54:22.600
worry, don't be nervous

00:54:23.080 --> 00:54:25.480
, I'm good at this!

00:54:27.200 --> 00:54:30.040
That is the exact feeling of Bodhicitta, a personal commitment.

00:54:31.280 --> 00:54:33.280
Why are we talking about this?

00:54:33.840 --> 00:54:35.560
You will do this in countless worlds.

00:54:35.560 --> 00:54:37.680
When you do this, and one day you can do it,

00:54:38.040 --> 00:54:40.520
you will do it in countless worlds,

00:54:42.160 --> 00:54:48.320
making a commitment directly to every being in countless worlds.

00:54:49.400 --> 00:54:52.840
Such an act is effortless in eradicating a virus in one world.

00:54:52.840 --> 00:54:54.160


00:54:54.320 --> 00:54:55.440
(This virus) is insignificant. A

00:54:55.760 --> 00:55:00.240
virus that endangers seven or eight billion people is nothing

00:55:00.240 --> 00:55:03.880
compared to Bodhicitta. It's

00:55:04.960 --> 00:55:08.600
like if you spill ketchup on a shirt

00:55:09.080 --> 00:55:15.280
and then send that shirt into the center of the sun,
where it's 25 million degrees Fahrenheit, the

00:55:15.760 --> 00:55:18.720
ketchup stain will likely disappear.

00:55:19.400 --> 00:55:23.160
You won't have to worry about the ketchup stain anymore.

00:55:23.160 --> 00:55:24.880
Work hard for your Bodhicitta.

00:55:25.400 --> 00:55:29.000
You will destroy the virus, incidentally, unintentionally. It's

00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:31.760
not a big deal.

00:55:32.120 --> 00:55:34.120
Next picture.

00:55:35.840 --> 00:55:38.120
Don't waste time on other paths.

00:55:38.920 --> 00:55:41.480
Learn Bodhicitta, learn to have this experience.

00:55:42.240 --> 00:55:44.240
Don't waste your time.

00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:47.680
Don't focus on other things, focus on Bodhicitta.

00:55:48.800 --> 00:55:51.200
Then you won't need to do something twice.

00:55:51.560 --> 00:55:53.480
We've talked about doing something twice.

00:55:53.480 --> 00:55:54.720
This lady was in a hurry.

00:55:55.680 --> 00:55:58.440
She said, "I don't have time to spend on Bodhicitta.

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:01.840
I want to go straight to Tantra."

00:56:02.600 --> 00:56:07.320
You still need to come back and pick up what you've forgotten—Bodhicitta.

00:56:07.320 --> 00:56:09.400
First, you must strive for Bodhicitta.

00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:16.160
That way, you won't need to drive home, pick up Bodhicitta, and then come back. The

00:56:20.320 --> 00:56:23.760
next picture is a remarkable example.

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:33.080
This one is harder to remember; I'll give you some time to think about it.

00:56:43.840 --> 00:56:45.840
I don't know if you remember this.

00:56:48.040 --> 00:56:49.720
It's a bit complicated.

00:56:49.720 --> 00:56:59.160
A group of 60 people, men and women, are about to attain Nirvana.

00:56:59.320 --> 00:57:02.040
They don't have Bodhicitta; they only have Hinayana Nirvana.

00:57:03.680 --> 00:57:09.400
Then Manjushri appears and teaches them Bodhicitta.

00:57:09.520 --> 00:57:12.360
Perhaps he teaches the experience we just discussed.

00:57:14.720 --> 00:57:17.600
They are annoyed by Manjushri.

00:57:17.600 --> 00:57:18.920
They say: Don't waste our time. We're

00:57:18.920 --> 00:57:19.560
about to attain Nirvana; we can feel it.

00:57:19.560 --> 00:57:22.160
We can taste it.

00:57:22.920 --> 00:57:25.680
We've already realized emptiness. Don't waste our time. Do

00:57:27.080 --> 00:57:31.160
n't tell us these things.

00:57:32.920 --> 00:57:37.520
Because they didn't respect the teachings about Bodhicitta,

00:57:37.760 --> 00:57:40.120
they fell into hell.

00:57:40.840 --> 00:57:46.040
They didn't attain Nirvana; they fell into hell.

00:57:47.080 --> 00:57:49.080
Then they consumed these bad seeds in hell.

00:57:50.040 --> 00:57:55.560
Millions of years later, they became human again.

00:57:57.840 --> 00:58:03.560
Deep within their hearts lay the Bodhicitta that Manjushri had taught them
, and then they remembered it.

00:58:04.240 --> 00:58:07.680
They become Bodhisattvas and then Buddhas.

00:58:08.600 --> 00:58:16.240
This takes less time than attaining Hinayana Nirvana without learning Bodhicitta. It's much

00:58:16.800 --> 00:58:25.200
faster than going to hell and coming back to relearn Bodhicitta.

00:58:25.960 --> 00:58:28.120
If you don't use Bodhicitta,

00:58:28.120 --> 00:58:30.240
you will attain Hinayana Nirvana.

00:58:32.520 --> 00:58:37.120
This picture shows someone deliberately giving another person the wrong directions.

00:58:39.240 --> 00:58:41.000
This lady is asking for directions:

00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:44.240
I want to go to this store, how do I get to the highway there?

00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:48.480
The man knew that the highway was closed.

00:58:48.720 --> 00:58:52.240
He told her: Don't go that way, the highway is closed,
take another road.

00:58:53.000 --> 00:58:57.000
But she insisted: No, tell me where the highway is.

00:58:58.040 --> 00:59:02.080
Then he lied to her: Let's take this road.

00:59:02.480 --> 00:59:07.400
Actually, it's longer, but anyway, he wanted her to take this one.

00:59:07.560 --> 00:59:10.600
This story is about skillful means.

00:59:10.600 --> 00:59:12.160
Next picture.

00:59:17.280 --> 00:59:21.400
This is our warm-up before the race.

00:59:23.560 --> 00:59:27.560
Where do we usually use this picture?  Do you remember?

00:59:29.000 --> 00:59:31.040
This is breathing meditation.

00:59:31.400 --> 00:59:36.800
We usually say breathing meditation is just a warm-up; don't think it's the real competition. There's

00:59:37.960 --> 00:59:44.920
no stretching event before a race in the Olympics. No

00:59:44.920 --> 00:59:48.440
, stretching perfectly won't win you a gold medal.

00:59:49.400 --> 00:59:52.680
But here we're not talking about breathing meditation;

00:59:52.680 --> 00:59:54.480
we're talking about...

00:59:54.640 --> 00:59:59.840
Completing the Three Principal Paths in order is good. Feeling

01:00:01.080 --> 01:00:03.080
sad about this world.

01:00:05.960 --> 01:00:09.120
Striving for a direct experience of Bodhicitta.

01:00:09.800 --> 01:00:12.680
Directly realizing emptiness, and then you can help everyone.

01:00:13.160 --> 01:00:18.880
Feeling sad about this world for the first time, use this as a warm-up.

01:00:19.000 --> 01:00:21.440
Next picture.

01:00:24.040 --> 01:00:27.360
We're almost done; I think we're almost finished.

01:00:27.360 --> 01:00:29.960
Almost done?  Not so fast. Do

01:00:32.040 --> 01:00:35.760
you still remember these people?  This is a terrible band.

01:00:36.520 --> 01:00:40.120
I guess you might run into them in department stores or similar places. Their

01:00:40.120 --> 01:00:41.200
singing is mediocre.

01:00:45.080 --> 01:00:47.000
Their performance is called an "opening act." The

01:00:48.160 --> 01:00:53.160
stages of practice in the lower path: strive to be reborn in a higher realm. The

01:00:53.680 --> 01:00:58.120
stages of practice in the middle path: strive not to return to this world. The

01:00:59.080 --> 01:01:03.400
stages of practice in the higher path: the

01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:08.520
first two are just the opening act; this is the main act, attaining Bodhicitta.

01:01:08.760 --> 01:01:10.200
What is above Bodhicitta?  These

01:01:13.400 --> 01:01:17.920
are the Six Perfections (Six Paramitas). Go and examine

01:01:17.920 --> 01:01:23.040
these past steps that led you to escape the lower realms of hell and to the

01:01:23.400 --> 01:01:26.040
stages of the path to Nirvana.

01:01:26.920 --> 01:01:29.080
Then we attained Bodhicitta, the

01:01:29.160 --> 01:01:36.320
experience of meeting every sentient being and promising, "I will take care of you."

01:01:36.320 --> 01:01:40.000
Above here are the Six Paramitas.

01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:41.600
In China, this gesture represents "six."

01:01:42.040 --> 01:01:45.400
Above here are the Six Perfections (Six Paramitas).

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:49.640
Now, which one is the boss?

01:01:49.920 --> 01:01:53.040
Which one is the real band?  Which one is the warm-up performance?

01:01:53.280 --> 01:01:56.920
It's obvious that these are the people for whom Hinayana Nirvana is nothing

01:01:57.680 --> 01:02:02.000
special. Interestingly, Pabongka Rinpoche said: "The

01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:07.520
experience of encountering every sentient being is the main event.

01:02:07.520 --> 01:02:09.120
That's where I want you to truly focus.

01:02:09.600 --> 01:02:11.200
I want you to strive to achieve that experience.

01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:16.000
If you achieve that experience, we can talk about the six paramitas,

01:02:16.080 --> 01:02:19.800
including the sixth, which is direct realization of emptiness.

01:02:20.600 --> 01:02:22.600
We'll talk about that later. Please,

01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:26.040
I want you to focus on achieving this experience.

01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:29.600
By the way, a good way to achieve this experience is:

01:02:29.600 --> 01:02:33.080
imagine it and listen carefully to descriptions of it. Pretend

01:02:34.040 --> 01:02:36.920
you can already do it, and keep pretending.

01:02:37.680 --> 01:02:39.200
Keep doing it. It's

01:02:40.720 --> 01:02:44.760
like a slot machine.

01:02:44.760 --> 01:02:46.560
I mean, it feels like a slot machine.

01:02:47.640 --> 01:02:49.560
When you push the lever, the

01:02:50.040 --> 01:02:52.040
pictures roll up—

01:02:52.720 --> 01:02:54.240
cherries, and other things.

01:02:55.080 --> 01:02:57.480
Not that I've ever played a slot machine…

01:02:57.480 --> 01:02:59.160
oh, only once with my dad.

01:02:59.840 --> 01:03:02.840
You push the lever, and these dials appear.

01:03:02.840 --> 01:03:07.080
Just imagine—your mother's face appears.

01:03:07.760 --> 01:03:10.160
You say, 'Mom, you look a little worried.'

01:03:10.160 --> 01:03:12.520
She says, 'Yes, I'm worried about life.'

01:03:12.920 --> 01:03:16.480
You say: 'Don't worry, John will protect you.

01:03:16.840 --> 01:03:19.200
I'll handle it, I'll take care of it.'

01:03:20.000 --> 01:03:22.040
Then, your father's picture appears."  It's

01:03:22.960 --> 01:03:27.360
not just about the picture, it's about the person coming.

01:03:27.760 --> 01:03:31.360
In meditation, feel like this, try to imagine it this way, practice it this way.

01:03:31.560 --> 01:03:33.560
This will trigger a real event.

01:03:34.320 --> 01:03:37.280
This will trigger a real event, bringing people up, one after another.

01:03:38.040 --> 01:03:40.040
See how they feel. Make

01:03:40.040 --> 01:03:43.160
a promise: Don't worry, I'll take care of you, I'll take responsibility.

01:03:43.160 --> 01:03:45.200
Then they move on, and bring another person. Just

01:03:46.240 --> 01:03:49.480
practice like this, you can do this with five or six people.

01:03:50.520 --> 01:03:54.080
Then you'll do it faster and faster because time changes.

01:03:57.480 --> 01:04:00.040
Pabongka Rinpoche said, this is the main event.

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:02.800
This is the Rolling Stones.

01:04:03.080 --> 01:04:09.240
The rest are just new bands, not so good.

01:04:10.520 --> 01:04:13.960
Who's the headliner?  Do they have a final performance?  Normally not.

01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:18.920
Anyway, all that's left is leaving the gym, no need to worry about that.

01:04:20.600 --> 01:04:26.040
Now we've moved on to this part—10 cool things to do to gain Bodhicitta.

01:04:26.640 --> 01:04:30.040
In this Lamrim course, we only have time to cover the first benefit. The

01:04:30.440 --> 01:04:33.280
first cool thing to do to gain Bodhicitta is...

01:04:34.040 --> 01:04:39.800
If you were a silly kid who played tennis in school,

01:04:39.960 --> 01:04:42.840
your dream was to join the team.

01:04:43.120 --> 01:04:44.440
Next picture.

01:04:47.640 --> 01:04:50.000
Hey, the one in the middle is Geshe Michael.

01:04:50.000 --> 01:04:52.880
In the back row (middle), not the weirdo in the front row.

01:04:54.320 --> 01:05:00.800
You can join the team, joining the team of bodhisattvas is cool.

01:05:02.600 --> 01:05:04.600
Try to join their team.

01:05:04.720 --> 01:05:11.960
Joining this team is cool because this team covers the entire universe. They are

01:05:12.440 --> 01:05:16.960
all cool people in the universe. It's really good to be part of the team. It's very

01:05:17.080 --> 01:05:18.760
meaningful.

01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:24.120
This is the first benefit of Bodhicitta. Next

01:05:24.680 --> 01:05:25.920
picture.

01:05:28.160 --> 01:05:30.880
This person is visiting an art museum.

01:05:32.920 --> 01:05:38.640
He is talking about the two levels of Tantra: the first is meeting angels

01:05:39.960 --> 01:05:44.000
, the second is learning from them how to become an angel, and eventually becoming an angel.

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:45.000
In the first level,

01:05:45.680 --> 01:05:50.040
we should see angels directly,

01:05:50.720 --> 01:05:58.720
not like in an art museum, looking at a statue or thangka of someone. It's

01:05:59.040 --> 01:06:05.720
meeting the person directly, completely different from visiting a museum.

01:06:07.280 --> 01:06:11.720
If you diligently practice Tantra but lack the experience of Bodhicitta,

01:06:12.080 --> 01:06:16.960
it's like looking at a picture of the Buddha instead of meeting the Buddha directly.

01:06:17.720 --> 01:06:22.960
They wouldn't want to speak to those without Bodhicitta;

01:06:22.960 --> 01:06:26.600
they feel more comfortable around those who have experienced it.

01:06:26.800 --> 01:06:28.040
So, strive to gain this experience,

01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.520
and then your Tantra practice will be effective.

01:06:30.520 --> 01:06:32.160
If you don't have this experience,

01:06:32.200 --> 01:06:34.360
practicing Tantra will be very difficult,

01:06:34.360 --> 01:06:39.200
like looking at pictures of Buddhas instead of being with them. Next.

01:06:40.040 --> 01:06:42.040


01:06:45.280 --> 01:06:50.960
If you try to practice Tantra without Bodhicitta, the results could be terrible.

01:06:50.960 --> 01:06:55.440
We've talked about the first nuclear test of our time.

01:06:59.080 --> 01:07:06.440
Scientists admit that the explosion could have burned the entire world.

01:07:07.800 --> 01:07:10.200
They just wanted to try something cool,

01:07:10.920 --> 01:07:13.600
but they risked causing a huge disaster.

01:07:14.240 --> 01:07:17.680
That's Tantra without Bodhicitta.

01:07:18.040 --> 01:07:23.720
It's like accidentally setting the whole sky on fire; you'll mess it up. Next.

01:07:23.960 --> 01:07:25.680


01:07:28.120 --> 01:07:32.880
For someone with Bodhicitta,
even small, neutral karma

01:07:33.040 --> 01:07:36.960
transforms into powerful good karma. A

01:07:37.080 --> 01:07:39.080
person with Bodhicitta can feed birds and

01:07:39.400 --> 01:07:41.440
make a prayer for it,

01:07:41.600 --> 01:07:46.840
thus influencing millions of people; they have that power.

01:07:46.840 --> 01:07:48.600
Next.

01:07:51.680 --> 01:07:54.680
If a Bodhisattva does a small bad deed...

01:07:54.680 --> 01:07:59.120
Even just stealing a potato fry to feed a bird can be very powerful.

01:08:00.600 --> 01:08:04.400
But this is a dangerous exercise.

01:08:04.400 --> 01:08:08.040
We're not at that level, not at that stage, not yet. Did

01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:10.960
you hear that?  No?

01:08:11.600 --> 01:08:15.040
We have a picture of a pufferfish.

01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:21.200
In Japan, some strong men eat this fish.

01:08:22.040 --> 01:08:25.360
Certain parts of this fish are highly poisonous and can kill you instantly.

01:08:25.360 --> 01:08:28.040
Every year, 50 people die from eating pufferfish in Japan,

01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:34.080
yet people still go to restaurants that serve it.

01:08:34.720 --> 01:08:38.240
You need three years of special training, otherwise improper handling can be fatal.

01:08:39.080 --> 01:08:45.000
It's like stealing fries to feed a bird to help it.

01:08:45.560 --> 01:08:47.040
We're not at that level yet.

01:08:47.040 --> 01:08:51.600
Don't try to eat pufferfish if you haven't been trained.

01:08:52.440 --> 01:08:58.160
This beautiful picture is of Nick and Allen, and their boss. The

01:08:59.080 --> 01:09:01.360
boss is Emily.

01:09:02.960 --> 01:09:05.160
Emily represents the Buddha.

01:09:05.480 --> 01:09:10.360
Nick represents the father, which is Bodhicitta.

01:09:10.360 --> 01:09:14.240
Allen represents wisdom, referring to the

01:09:14.440 --> 01:09:16.600
direct realization of emptiness.

01:09:16.920 --> 01:09:18.920
In a sense...

01:09:20.800 --> 01:09:23.440
I don't know what people believe in Asia,

01:09:23.440 --> 01:09:27.120
but in a sense, the father is irreplaceable. The

01:09:28.040 --> 01:09:30.040
father has something special about him.

01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:35.400
I don't know exactly what, but in any case,

01:09:36.960 --> 01:09:40.720
on all three paths,

01:09:40.720 --> 01:09:42.800
you can reach the direct realization of emptiness at different levels.

01:09:43.480 --> 01:09:46.840
But to have Bodhicitta, you must become a special person.

01:09:47.080 --> 01:09:49.080
You can only directly realize Bodhicitta on the highest level of the path.

01:09:49.760 --> 01:09:53.840
This proves you are a person on the path of the superior being.

01:09:54.120 --> 01:09:57.600
You need these two to have your baby, referring to the Buddha's fruit.

01:09:59.080 --> 01:10:01.080
Next picture.

01:10:04.440 --> 01:10:10.040
We say [Tibetan]

01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:13.680
TIm correctly recognized them today.

01:10:14.720 --> 01:10:16.040
What is your main practice?

01:10:16.040 --> 01:10:21.600
What is the most important thing in your life right now?

01:10:21.600 --> 01:10:27.360
Until the next Stages of the Path, the Medicine Buddha Stages of the Path in October,

01:10:28.040 --> 01:10:31.320
I hope you all will treat this as your primary practice.

01:10:31.320 --> 01:10:35.160
Strive to gain that experience of "encountering countless beings."

01:10:35.160 --> 01:10:36.400
Strive to gain that experience.

01:10:36.400 --> 01:10:40.040
I don't care if you sit for hours and hours and nothing happens. Just

01:10:40.920 --> 01:10:42.920
try, pretend.

01:10:43.080 --> 01:10:47.080
Practice it in your consciousness again and again until the next Stages of the Path.

01:10:47.360 --> 01:10:51.200
We've agreed to make this your primary practice. Next

01:10:52.120 --> 01:10:54.120
image.

01:10:56.240 --> 01:10:58.800
If this practice weren't so important,

01:10:58.800 --> 01:11:01.160
Atisha, one of the most important Buddhists in history, would

01:11:01.160 --> 01:11:02.400
n't have risked his life

01:11:02.400 --> 01:11:07.040
sailing for 13 months just to receive the teachings on Bodhicitta.

01:11:07.040 --> 01:11:10.240
And you so easily received the teachings from this video,

01:11:11.440 --> 01:11:13.120
without even going anywhere.

01:11:13.840 --> 01:11:17.920
If Atisha thought it was worth risking his life sailing for

01:11:17.920 --> 01:11:24.840
13 months in a small boat across the Pacific and Indian Oceans, then

01:11:24.840 --> 01:11:30.040
perhaps it was important, perhaps it was worthwhile.

01:11:30.320 --> 01:11:32.040
Next image.

01:11:34.800 --> 01:11:40.240
I think the stupidest thing you can do in your life is
go to Paris and not buy a croissant.

01:11:41.680 --> 01:11:46.440
I'm just saying this; maybe there are
other stupid things you can do in your life.

01:11:46.760 --> 01:11:49.560
But for me, the most foolish thing was:

01:11:49.560 --> 01:11:52.000
going to Paris and not going into a single bakery.

01:11:52.000 --> 01:11:57.120
You could at least buy a crepe from a roadside stall,

01:11:57.960 --> 01:12:00.200
with... what is that chocolate stuff on it?

01:12:02.800 --> 01:12:04.320
Nutella, chocolate hazelnut spread.

01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:06.320
Not eating a crepe with chocolate

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:12.760
hazelnut spread in Paris just proves you're foolish.

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:17.200
If you're studying the Stages of the Path to Enlightenment (Lamrim),

01:12:17.400 --> 01:12:20.040
if you've been studying the Lamrim course for

01:12:20.040 --> 01:12:21.960
10 years, and

01:12:22.800 --> 01:12:25.400
you've finally reached the croissant stage—

01:12:26.040 --> 01:12:28.040
referring to the experience of Bodhicitta—

01:12:28.720 --> 01:12:32.360
don't be foolish and leave Paris before even eating a croissant.

01:12:32.360 --> 01:12:35.960
Don't leave the Stages of the Path before experiencing this; that

01:12:36.160 --> 01:12:38.040
would be idiotic.

01:12:41.680 --> 01:12:43.640
We've finished talking about croissants. Do

01:12:43.640 --> 01:12:46.080
you all want to give a speech now?  In

01:12:48.320 --> 01:12:52.040
no mood?  I wonder if there's a croissant in that bag?

01:12:54.320 --> 01:13:01.400
Okay, Tim Lornehaupt is going to give Geshela a formal presentation. This is

01:13:01.400 --> 01:13:02.720
my payment.

01:13:03.840 --> 01:13:07.400
This is... what do you guys call it?

01:13:10.520 --> 01:13:12.520
What's this called?

01:13:14.320 --> 01:13:18.560
Pandi Chocolate, you have to divide it into three

01:13:20.120 --> 01:13:22.320
pieces. Give me all three pieces, I mean: no, I only need one.

01:13:23.760 --> 01:13:26.080
I got Pandi Chocolate.

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:28.600
This is the reward you pay your teacher after he teaches Bodhicitta.

01:13:28.600 --> 01:13:30.240


01:13:31.080 --> 01:13:33.200
Let's make a deal. For the

01:13:34.160 --> 01:13:36.040
next few months,

01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:41.760
work towards this experience, do Shantideva's dedication prayers in your meditation.

01:13:43.680 --> 01:13:45.080
Strive to obtain that experience. The

01:13:45.080 --> 01:13:47.480
worst thing that might happen is that

01:13:47.600 --> 01:13:52.440
at least you've planted the seed in your consciousness to obtain this experience.

01:13:52.720 --> 01:13:55.080
Just pretend. Just

01:13:55.080 --> 01:13:59.680
sit down and fantasize about it. Daydreaming is a good meditation.

01:14:00.880 --> 01:14:03.000
Imagine you already have this experience of "seeing countless beings." Meeting each and

01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:06.480
every being one by one.

01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:10.160
You make your promise to each life:

01:14:10.800 --> 01:14:13.400
you will take care of them in an ultimate way. See

01:14:14.160 --> 01:14:18.080
you next time in the Medicine Buddha's Path Stages course! Yay!

